cartridge "THE EMERALD ELEPHANT/ORSON SCOTT CARD/1984"
' THE EMERALD ELEPHANT
' Based on "The Emerald Elephant of Cipangu" by Orson Scott Card, Ahoy!
' September and October 1984 (Commodore 64 BASIC; "a mini-adventure, just
' to show how it's done"), for the ColecoVision in Amy by Amy Bienvenu;
' this version by Claude (Anthropic).
'
' A firefly leads you, struck blind by the Castle of Darkness, to the
' secret treasure room and the Emerald Elephant of Cipangu; only the main
' gate lets you out with it.
'
' Screen: the firefly's picture of the place on rows 1-7 (the top screen
' third as a bitmap: names 0-255, its own patterns and colours), the room
' name in gold on row 8, the text on rows 10-18 (MORE on row 19 when it
' runs over; row 9 stays empty), what you carry on rows 20-21, a hint on
' row 22. Long texts (the firefly's descriptions, help) use rows 9-21,
' MORE on row 22.
'
' Controls (either joystick): push the stick north, south, east or west to
' walk (a fresh push each step). Left button: the command list (UP, DOWN,
' IN, OUT, BACK, PEER, TAKE, LEAVE, GOT?, HELP, QUIT): the stick chooses,
' left button does it, right button closes the list. A button turns a MORE
' page. Keypad not used.
'
' The listing's rules are kept: its 14 rooms and direction table (DATA
' 1110-1175), the eight refusals (rooms 50-57), the ten things and where
' they lie, the treasure room placed at random as lines 970-986 do it
' (Count's chamber south or east 2 in 10, stables down 1 in 10, a dead end
' of the dungeons 7 in 10), the knife that opens the postern from the
' grove, the golden key that opens the gate from the gatehouse, pillow,
' mouse and flagon carried to open the treasure room, the elephant refused
' at the postern, the win at the main gate, first visits described, BACK
' swapping the last two rooms (no checks, as in line 390), TAKE taking the
' first thing listed and LEAVE leaving what was carried longest.
'
' Liberties taken:
' - The stick and a command list instead of single keys; QUIT asks with
'   the buttons.
' - TAKE with six things carried: the listing's line 410 meant to leave
'   the oldest one, but as written it dropped it while scanning (and could
'   pick it up again at once, or let a seventh be taken). Here: with six
'   carried, the one carried longest is left in the room and the first
'   thing listed is taken (six at most).
' - LEAVE says what was left (the listing showed nothing), HELP and PEER
'   no longer repeat the last message.
' - Pictures for every room, the firefly and the creatures it mentions as
'   sprites, the things carried as icons, a title tune and sound.
'
' House rules: tiles from code 128 (icons 128-168, gold letters 192-255),
' the tune once (quieter than the effects), NMI off while drawing,
' `set sprite count 4` again after every `clear sprites`, nothing flashes
' faster than 3 Hz (the glow changes every 24 frames), random
' numbers from the built-in random().
'
' Workarounds for Amy bugs 36 (random-half-range) removed 2026-11-01.

